The arrest on 2026-05-07 was a coordinated German and US effort on German charges rather than a BKA arrest: the case is investigated by the IRS-CI Cyber Crimes Unit and DEA Miami with substantial assistance from the Bundeskriminalamt Cybercrime Unit and the Zentrale Kriminalinspektion Oldenburg, while the FBI, USPIS and HSI belonged to the task force that investigated the marketplace from 2016 to 2022 ([US DEA, 2026-05-13](https://www.dea.gov/press-releases/2026/05/13/german-citizen-charged-laundering-funds-linked-prominent-darknet)). Only the US indictment accuses Andresen of being the main administrator; the German charges are concealment money laundering ([US DEA, 2026-05-13](https://www.dea.gov/press-releases/2026/05/13/german-citizen-charged-laundering-funds-linked-prominent-darknet); [The Record, 2026-05-13](https://therecord.media/dream-market-admin-arrested-in-germany)). The 2022 transfers went into new consolidated wallets, not a single wallet, and the searches located about $1.7 million of gold bars and over $23,000 in cash and identified bank accounts and wallets holding about $1.2 million, rather than seizing $1.2 million in cryptocurrency ([US DEA, 2026-05-13](https://www.dea.gov/press-releases/2026/05/13/german-citizen-charged-laundering-funds-linked-prominent-darknet)).
